<article class="env-lemma" id="0DDC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DDC">Lemma <span data-tag="0DDC">59.78.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $\mathcal{F}$ is a torsion abelian sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$, then $H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F})$ is a torsion abelian group for all $n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $K$ in $D^+(X_{\acute{e}tale})$ has torsion cohomology sheaves, then $H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, K)$ is a torsion abelian group for all $n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To prove (1) we write $\mathcal{F} = \bigcup \mathcal{F}[n]$ where $\mathcal{F}[d]$ is the $d$-torsion subsheaf. By Lemma <a href="/tag/03Q5" data-tag="03Q5">59.51.4</a> we have $H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}[d])$. This proves (1) as $H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}[d])$ is annihilated by $d$. 
    <p>
      To prove (2) we can use the spectral sequence $E_2^{p, q} = H^ p_{\acute{e}tale}(X, H^ q(K))$ converging to $H^ n_{\acute{e}tale}(X, K)$ (Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a>) and the result for sheaves. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>